$DATUM The oily mass of 4-dimethylaminoethoxybenzaldehyde, Raney-nickel (7.50
kg; 15%), and methanolic ammonia (300 L; 20% solution) were taken in a
pressure reactor and heated to 50-55 °C for 8 h at a hydrogen pressure of
8-10 kg/cm2. After completion of reaction as monitored by TLC, the
mixture was cooled to 25-30 °C and filtered. The filtrate was
concentrated under reduced pressure to provide a pure, viscous, oily
material. This was stored as a toluene solution. Yield: 63.63 kg. HPLC
purity ≥ 98%. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 1.35 (br s, 2H, NH2), 2.33 (s, 6H, CH3,
CH3), 2.72 (t, 2H, CH2), 3.80 (br s, 2H, CH2), 4.06 (t, 2H, CH2), 6.89
(d, 2H, CH, CH), 7.21 (d, 2H, CH, CH), mass:195 (M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Raney nickel used, 64 kg scale (product)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Improved Process for Trimethobenzamide Hydrochloride
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
