$DATUM 3-(3-Isopropylphenoxy)-N-[3-(1,1,2,2-tetrafluoroethoxy)-benzyl]aniline
(13e). To a solution of 16e (1.0 g, 4.4 mmol) and
3-(1,1,2,2-tetrafluoroethoxy)benzaldehyde (0.9 g, 4 mmol) in 20 mL of
dichloroethane were added sodium triacetoxyborohydride (1.1 g, 5.2 mmol)
and glacial acetic acid (0.3 mL, 4.8 mmol). The reaction mixture was
stirred at room temperature for 1.5 h, then quenched with saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 and extracted with diethyl ether. The organic layer was
washed with water and brine, dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo
to give 13e (1.73 g, 100%) as a brown oil, which was used without further
purification.
3-(3-Isopropylphenoxy)-N-[3-(1,1,2,2-tetrafluoroethoxy)-benzyl]aniline
(13e), yield (1.73 g, 100%). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.38 (t, 1H), 7.28 (t, 1H),
7.24 (d, 1H), 7.14 (t, 1H), 7.00 (d, 1H), 6.94 (m, 1H), 6.8 (dd, 2H),
6.42 (d, 1H), 6.34 (s, 1H), 6.10 (t, 1H), 5.92 (t, 1H), 5.74 (t, 1H),
4.38 (s, 2H), 3.78 (s, 1H), 2.90 (m, 1H), 1.22 (d, 6H). 19F NMR (CDCl3)
-88.7 (m, 2F), -137.3 (dt, 2F). HRMS calcd for C24H23F4NO2 434.1743 [M +
H]+, found 434.1736.
