$DATUM Compound S6421 (6.86 g, 0.029 mol), tert-butyl piperidin-4-ylcarbamate
(6.99 g, 0.035 mol) and titanium(IV) ethoxide were mixed in THF (30 mL)
and heated at 70°C for 4 hours. The reaction was cooled to room
temperature, filtered through a plug of celite and the clear filtrate
added to 2M NaOH(aq) (100 ml). The mixture was extracted with EtOAc (4 x
50 mL) and the organics were combined and washed with brine (30 mL) and
then concentrated to a crude, viscous yellow gel (11.7g). This was
dissolved in glacial acetic acid (90 ml) and zinc (7.61 g, 0.12 mol) was
added to the stirring solution. The reaction was stirred at room
temperature overnight. The mixture was then filtered through celite,
washed with NaHCO3 (aq) solution (2 x 100 mL) and purified by flash
chromatography using a MeOH & EtOAc gradient in DCM to give S65. Yellow
gel, yield 8.4 g, 68%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) 8.63 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H),
8.49 (dd, J = 1.4, 4.9 Hz, 1H), 7.68 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.47 (t, J =
8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.24 (dd, J = 5.1, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.15 (dd, J = 1.4, 8.4 Hz,
1H), 7.05 (dd, J = 1.9, 9.7 Hz, 1H), 5.34 (s, 1H), 4.00 (br. s., 2H),
2.73 (br. t, J = 11.9 Hz, 2H), 2.46 - 2.60 (m, 1H), 1.88 (br. t, J = 12.7
Hz, 2H), 1.44 (s, 9H), 1.22 - 1.33 (m, 2H).
