$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of
6-(4-(substituted-amino)phenyl)-4,5-dihydro-3(2H)-pyridazinones IIIa-h
Appropriate aldehyde IIa-h (1.58 mmol) was added to stirred solution of
6-(4-aminophenyl)-4,5-dihydropyridazin-3(2H)-one (I) (1.58 mmol) in
methanol (15 ml) with constant stirring. The reaction mixture was further
stirred at room temperature overnight. The suspension obtained was cooled
in ice and sodium borohydride (0.39 g) added in small amounts with
constant stirring for a period of 30 min and the solution obtained was
further stirred for 2 hr. Ice cold water was added to it and the
precipitated material was filtered off, washed with ice cold water,
dried, and recrystallization from a mixture of methanol and chloroform.
The formation of desired pyridazinones IIIa-h. The structures of these
compounds were elucidated by using various spectral and elemental
analyses.
6-(4-(3,4,5-Trimethoxybenzylamino)phenyl)-4,5-dihydropyridazin-3(2H)-one
(IIIb). Yield: 62.09%. m.p. 134-135°C. Spectroscopic analysis: IR (KBr) ν
max/ cm-1: 3360 (NH), 3069 (CH, aromatic), 2928 (CH, aliphatic), 1661
(C=O), 1600 (C=C, aromatic); 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz, δ, ppm): 2.58 (t,
2H, 4-CH2, J = 7.46 Hz), 2.95 (t, 2H, 5-CH2, J = 7.42 Hz), 3.84 (s, 9H,
3x-OCH3), 4.31 (s, 3H, NH-CH2), 6.58 (s, 2H, Ar-H), 6.65 (dd, 2H, Ar-H,
Jo = 6.88 Hz, Jm = 1.90 Hz), 7.58 (dd, 2H, Ar-H, Jo = 6.84 Hz, Jm = 1.90
Hz) and 8.36 (s, 1H,-NH, pyridazinone). Anal. calcd. for C20H23N3O4: C:
65.03, H: 6.27, N: 11.37%; found; C: 65.06, H: 6.14; N: 11.31%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of new pyridazinone derivatives as platelet aggregation
inhibitors
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Thota, Sridhar; Bansal, Ranju
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Medicinal Chemistry Research (2010), 19(8), 808-816

