$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Compound S6421 (6.86 g, 0.029 mol), tert-butyl
piperidin-4-ylcarbamate (6.99 g, 0.035 mol) and titanium(IV) ethoxide
were mixed in THF (30 mL) and heated at 70°C for 4 hours. The reaction
was cooled to room temperature, filtered through a plug of celite and the
clear filtrate added to 2M NaOH(aq) (100 ml). The mixture was extracted
with EtOAc (4 x 50 mL) and the organics were combined and washed with
brine (30 mL) and then concentrated to a crude, viscous yellow gel
(11.7g). This was dissolved in glacial acetic acid (90 ml) and zinc (7.61
g, 0.12 mol) was added to the stirring solution. The reaction was stirred
at room temperature overnight. The mixture was then filtered through
celite, washed with NaHCO3 (aq) solution (2 x 100 mL) and purified by
flash chromatography using a MeOH & EtOAc gradient in DCM to give S65. As
for the synthesis of S65 using S6721 (8.0 g, 31.8 mmol) and tert-butyl
piperidin-4-ylcarbamate (7.65 g, 38.2 mmol) giving S68 as a yellow oil
(6.55 g, 52%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) 8.64 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 8.50
(dd, J = 1.2, 4.7 Hz, 1H), 7.68 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.57 - 7.61 (m, 2H),
7.50 - 7.55 (m, 2H), 7.22 - 7.26 (m, 1H), 5.12 (s, 1H), 4.01 (br. s.,
2H), 2.71 (t, J = 11.2 Hz, 2H), 2.50 - 2.59 (m, 1H), 1.90 (d, J = 11.0
Hz, 2H), 1.45 (s, 9H), 1.20 - 1.37 (m, 2H); LCMS [M+H] = 436.4; HPLC
(water/ACN + 0.1% TFA gradient) 97.8% at 254nm.
