$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of
2-(4-((2-chloro-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-6-yl)methyl)piperazin-1-yl)-2-methylpropanamide
(32) A suspension of 2-piperazin-1-yl-isobutyramide dihydrochloride
(57.5g, 235mmol) in anhydrous DCM (1.8L) was treated with triethylamine
(66ml, 471mmol) and stirred for 5min at room temperature under a nitrogen
atmosphere.
2-Chloro-4-morpholin-4-yl-thieno[3,2-d]pyrimidine-6-carbaldehyde19 (31)
(44.6g, 157mmol) was then added followed by acetic acid (9ml, 157mmol)
and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (43.2g, 203mmol). The reaction was
stirred at room temperature over the weekend. Sat. Sodium hydrogen
carbonate (1L) was carefully added and the product extracted into DCM
(3x1L). The DCM extracts were combined, dried (MgSO4), filtered and
evaporated to afford an orange solid. The crude product was purified by
triturating with hot methanol (500ml), filtering hot and the solid dried
in vacuo to afford
2-(4-((2-chloro-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-6-yl)methyl)piperazin-1-yl)-2-methylpropanamide
(32). cream solid, yield 31.7g, 46%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ(s, 1H),
7.05 (br d , 1H ), 5.5 (br d 1H), 4.0 (m, 4H), 3.9 (m , 4H), 3.85 (s ,
2H, ), 2.6(br s , 8H), 1.3 (s , 6H).
