$DATUM N-[3-(1,1,2,2-Tetrafluoroethoxy)benzyl]-3-[(3-trifluoromethoxy)
phenoxy]aniline (13c). To a solution of 16c (1.0 g, 3.7 mmol) and
3-(1,1,2,2-tetrafluoroethoxy)benzaldehyde (0.83 g, 3.7 mmol) in 18.5 mL
of dichloroethane were added sodium triacetoxyborohydride (1.0 g, 4.7
mmol) and glacial acetic acid (0.25 mL, 4.3 mmol). The reaction mixture
was stirred at room-temperature overnight, then quenched with saturated
aqueous sodium bicarbonate and extracted with methylene chloride. The
organic layer was dried over anhyd MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo to
give 13c (1.8 g, 100%) as a yellow oil, which was greater than 92% pure
by reverse phase HPLC analysis.
N-[3-(1,1,2,2-Tetrafluoroethoxy)benzyl]-3-[(3-trifluoromethoxy)
phenoxy]aniline (13c), yield (1.8 g, 100%). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.33-7.21
(m, 3H), 7.18 (m, 3H), 6.93 (m, 2H), 6.88 (d, 1H), 6.42 (dd, 1H), 6.39
(dd, 1H), 6.28 (s, 1H), 5.89 (t, 1H), 4.34 (s, 2H). 19F NMR (CDCl3) δ
-58.2 (s, 3F), -88.4 (m, 2F), -137.1 (dt, 2F). HRMS calcd for C22H17F7NO3
476.1097 [M + H]+, found 476.1069.
