After the mixture was stirred for 1 h, NaBH(OAc)3 (8.29 g, 39.1 mmol) was
added portionwise and the mixture was stirred for 48 h at room
temperature. The reaction mixture was quenched with a saturated solution
of NaHCO3 at 0 °C and extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 100 mL). The
combined organic layer was dried over Na2SO4, and the solvent was removed
under reduced pressure. Crude product was purified by column
chromatography (EtOAc/MeOH, 20:1) to give compound 7.
(S)-4-{2-[(2-Amino-4,5,6,7-tetrahydrobenzothiazol-6-yl)-propylamino]ethyl}piperazine-1-carboxylic
