$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2’-O-{3-[(3-quinolinylmethyl)amino]propyl}-9-deoxo-9a-methyl-9a-aza-9a-homoerythromycin
A (26b) To a solution of 7 (1g, 1.24 mmol) in MeOH (35 mL) triethylamine
(0.585 mL, 4.2 mmol) and 3-quinolinecarbaldehyde (164 mg, 1.04 mmol) were
added and reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature 18 hours when
NaBH4 (94 mg, 2.48 mmol) was added. Reaction mixture was stirred for
additionally 3 hours when solvent was evaporated. Residue obtained after
evaporation of the solvent was dissolved in water, pH adjusted to 9.5,
and extracted with DCM. Combined organic layers were dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4. Evaporation of the solvent yielded 1.2 g of yellow powder product
which was further purified by column chromatography (eluent
DCM:MeOH:NH4OH=90:9:1.5). 0.14 g (12 %) of the title product. MS (ES+):
947.5 [MH]+. 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6 ) δ ppm: 0.77-0.82 (m, 6H),
0.90-0.95 (m, 6H), 1.00 (s, 3H), 1.02-1.03 (m, 1H), 1.04 (d, J=6.1 Hz,
3H), 1.08 (d, J=7.5 Hz, 3H), 1.09 (s, 3H), 1.13 (d, J=6.1 Hz, 3H), 1.15
