$DATUM (2S,4S)-tert-butyl
2-(isoindoline-2-carbonyl)-4-(quinolin-4-ylmethylamino)pyrrolidine-1-
carboxylate, 15a In a 25 mL round-bottomed flask was dissolved
(2S,4S)-tert-butyl 4-amino-2-(isoindoline-2-
carbonyl)pyrrolidine-1-carboxylate (0.135 g, 0.407 mmol) in DCM (4 ml)
and acetic acid (0.073 ml, 1.283 mmol) to give a colorless solution.
0.611 mmol of the desired aldehydes (Quinoline-4- carboxaldehyde or
2-methoxy-1-naphthaldehyde, 1.1 eq.) and molecular sieves (3Å) were
added.The reaction was stirred overnight at room temperature. Sodium
cyanotrihydroborate (0.035 g, 0.550 mmol) was added. The reaction was
stirred overnight at roomtemperature. Next, 2g of celite was added and
after filtration over a small Celite filter, the solvent was evaporated
under reduced pressure. The crude residue was redissolved in EtOAc and
washed with 1M NaOH. The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4, filtered
and concentrated yielding the secondary amines which were further
purified using gradient-elution-type flash chromatography (hexanes to
ethyl acetate/methanol). 15a Yield: 37% 15a 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
8.89-8.87(t, J=4Hz, 1H), 8.15-8.08(m, 2H), 7.73-7.70(m, 1H), 7.59-
7.52(m, 2H), 7.34-7.23(m, 4H), 5.27-5.01(dd, J=13.2Hz, 90.4Hz, 1H),
4.93-4.77(m, 3H), 4.69- 4.54(m, 1H), 4.37-4.22(m, 2H), 3.94-3.86(m, 1H),
3.83-3.66(m, 3H), 3.55-3.46(m, 1H), 2.55- 2.44(m, 1H) ESI+-MS m/z= 473.2
[M+H], 495.2[M+Na]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM molecular sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
