$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of
5-{[2,3-dihydro-[1,4]-benzodioxin)-6-ylmethyl]amino}-N-(2-[2-dimethyl
amino)ethyl]-1H-benzo[de]isoquinolin-1,3(2H)-dione. 400 mg of amonafide
(1.41x10-3 mol, 1 eq), 15 mL of toluene and 280 mg of intermediate
(5-{[(1Z)-benzo(3,5-bis(acetyloxy)-2-[(acetyloxy)methyl]-6-oxy-tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-ylacetate)-5-ylmethylene]amino}-N-(2-[2-dimethylamino)ethyl]-1H-benzo
[de]iso quinolin-1,3(2H)-dione) (1.2 equivalents) were refluxed for 16
hours. After cooling, the toluene was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue of the intermediate (2-[2-
dimethylamino)ethyl]-{[(1Z)-(2,3-dihydro-[1,4]-benzodioxin)-6-ylmethylene]amino}-1H-benzo
[de]isoquinolin-1,3(2H)-dione) was directly submitted to the next
reaction. 610 mg of intermediate
(5-{[2-(2-phenoxy-)-6-hydroxymethyltetrahydropyran-3,4,5-triacetoxy)-5-yl
methyl]amino}-N-(2-[2-dimethylamino)ethyl]-1H-benzo[de]isoquinolin-1,3(2H)-dione),
10 mL of anhydrous methanol and 177 mg of NaBH3CN (2 equivalents) were
stirred for 2 hours. A saturated aqueous sodium chloride solution was
added and then the reaction mixture extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic
phase was evaporated under reduced pressure and the residue was submitted
to flash chromatography with CH2Cl2/MeOH (90:10 v/v), followed by a
second chromatography step (on a RP-C18 column eluted with a linear
gradient solvent system starting with MeOH/H2O (80:20 v/v) and
progressing to 100% MeOH. This resulted in the isolation of
5-{[2,3-dihydro-[1,4]-benzodioxin)-6-ylmethyl]amino}-N-(2-[2-dimethylamino)ethyl]-1H-benzo[de]isoquinolin-1,3(2H)-dione
yield 325 mg (431.50g/mol, 7.53x10-4 mol), 53.0%. C25H25N3O4. 1H NMR
(D6-DMSO) : δ = 2.21 (6H, s, H3C-15 and H3C-16), 2.50-2.55 (2H, m,
H2C-14), 4.13 (2H, t, J = 6.8 Hz, H2C-13), 4.20 (2H, s, OCH2CH2O), 4.32
(2H, d, J = 5.7 Hz, H- 18), 6.82 (1H, d, J = 8.4 Hz, H2C-23), 6.89 (2H,
dd, J = 8.4 and 2.1 Hz, H24, OCH2CH2O), 6.92 (1H, s, HC-20), 7.14 (1H, t,
J = 6.0 Hz, NH-17), 7.17 (1H, d, J = 2.7 Hz, H-4), 7.59 (1H, t, J = 7.8
Hz, H-7), 8.00 (1H, d, J = 7.8 Hz, H-6), 8.03 (1H, d, J = 2.7 Hz, H-2),
8.04 (1H, d, J = 7.8 Hz, H- 8). 13C NMR (D6-DMSO): δ = 37.4 (C-13), 45.3
(C-15 and C-16), 45.6 (C-18), 56.4 (C-14), 64.0 and 63.9 (C-25 and C-26),
108.5, 115.8, 116.9, 120.0, 120.5, 121.6, 121.9, 122.3, 125.3, 127.0,
131.6, 131.9, 133.5, 142.2, 143.2, 147.1, 163.6 and 163.4 (C-11 and
C-12). EI-MS : 58 (100); 71 (82); 149 (86); 360 (54) and 431 (5).
