$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step E. To a solution of
6-amino-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one (0.050 g,
0.229 mmol) in MeOH (3 mL) and AcOH (0.3 mL) was added
3-oxo-azetidine-1-carboxylic acid tert-butyl ester (0.780 g, 0.450 mmol)
and the reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 1 h.
NaBH3CN (0.052 g, 0.825 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was
stirred at ambient temperature for 16 h. The reaction mixture was
concentrated in vacuo and the residue was purified by preparative-HPLC
(Table 3, Method 2). Method 2: Column: YMC-pack ODS-AQ 150x30 mm, 5 μm.
Mobile phase: acetonitrile in water (0.05% hydrochloric acid solution),
from 27% to 57% in 11 min; Flow rate: 25 mL/min. Wavelength: 220 nm.
6-[(Piperidin-4-ylmethyl)-amino]-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one
hydrochloride acid (15j). Prepared according to the procedure of compound
15a (Step E) from 4-formyl-piperidine-1-carboxylic acid tert-butyl ester
(2 equiv) and NaBH3CN (5 equiv) at ambient temperature for 0.5 h; 0.0231
g, 32%, as a white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD): δ 7.03 (m, 1H), 6.80
(m, 2H), 4.60 (s, 2H), 4.31 (s, 2H), 3.45 (m, 4H), 3.02 (m, 2H), 2.09 (m,
3H), 1.54 (m, 2H). LC/MS (Table 1, Method 7) Rt = 1.435 min.; MS m/z: 316
[M+H]+.
