$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM In a 500 mL three-neck flask equipped with a mechanical stirrer, nitrogen
inlet, and a thermocouple were placed 8.25 g (25.2 mmol) of the ketone
8b, 9.80 g (28.4 mmol) of the pyrazole salt 10, and 124 mL of
dimethylacetamide. The resulting homogeneous solution was cooled to −10
°C, and 6.94 g (32.7 mmol) of sodium triacetoxyborohydride was added
portionwise. The resulting mixture was stirred for 2 h and quenched by
the slow addition of a mixture of NH4OH (8.3 mL) and water (16.5 mL). The
slurry was heated to 50 °C and then cooled to 22 °C and filtered. The wet
cake was washed with 5:1 dimethylacetamide/water (65 mL) and then water
(65 mL) and dried under vacuum/N2 sweep to afford the title compound
(11). The product was used in the next step without further purification.
Off white solid, yield 10.6 g, 94%. LC−MS: 499.10 (M + 1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Omarigliptin (MK-3102): A Novel Long-Acting DPP-4 Inhibitor for
Once-Weekly Treatment of Type 2 Diabetes
