$DATUM Ethyl
2-methyl-2-[(4-{[({4-methyl-2-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-1,3-thiazol-5-
yl}methyl)amino]methyl}phenyl)oxy]propanoate (22) A solution of 21
(1.36g, 5.7mmol) in dichloroethane (20mL) was treated at room temperature
with sodium triacetoxyborohydride (2.03g, 2eq) and acetic acid (0.43g,
1.5eq) then a solution of 5 (1.3g, 4.8mmol) in dichloroethane (10mL) was
added dropwise. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 24h then
evaporated to dryness. The residue was taken up with water, acidified
with 1N HCl and then neutralized with 1N NaHCO3. The mixture was then
extracted with CH2Cl2 and the combined organic layers were dried over
Na2SO4, filtered and the solvent removed under vacuum to afford the crude
product. Purification by chromatograpy, eluting with CH2Cl2 /MeOH (99 :1)
gave 22 as a clear oil (300mg, 13%) Ethyl
2-methyl-2-[(4-{[({4-methyl-2-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-1,3-thiazol-5-
yl}methyl)amino]methyl}phenyl)oxy]propanoate (22), Yield (300mg, 13%) 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3 ) : δ 7.99(d, J=10.8Hz, 2H), 7.65 (d, J=10.8Hz, 2H),
7.20 (d, J=10.8Hz, 2H), 6.82 (d, J=10.8Hz, 2H), 4.23 (q, J=7.2 Hz, 2H),
3.91 (s, 2H), 3.77 (s, 2H), 2.37 (s, 3H), 1.58 (s, 6H), 1.25 (t, J=7.2Hz,
3H).
