$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of methyl
thieno[3,2-c]pyridine-2-carboxylate (15 g, 77.6 mmol) in anhydrous THF
(250 mL) was added LiA4 (4.42 g, 116.4 mmol) in portions at 0 °C. The
suspension was stirred at 0 °C for 1h, then quenched by saturated aqueous
NH4Cl and filtered. The filtrate was washed with brine and concentrated.
The residue was used in the next step without any further purification
(10.3 g). To a flame-dried round-bottomed flask containing above residue
(3.2 g, 19.4 mmol) was added DPPA (8 g, 29.1 mmol) in THF (50 mL). The
reaction mixture was stirred for 5 min and cooled to 0°C, followed by
adding DBU (4.43 g, 29.1 mmol) via syringe. The mixture was stirred at
reflux overnight. The reaction was then partitioned between water and
ethyl ether. The aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl ether. The
combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4,
concentrated, and purified by chromatography to afford
2-(azidomethyl)thieno[3,2-c]pyridine (3.27 g). Yield: 89%. To a solution
of 2-(azidomethyl)thieno[3,2-c]pyridine (3 g, 15.8 mmol) in anhydrous THF
(50 mL) was added Ph3P (8.27 g, 31.5 mmol), followed by NH4OH (2 mL). The
solution was stirred at rt. overnight. Solvent was removed, and the
residue was purified by chromatography to afford the title compound (2.5
g). Yield: 97%. 1-(imidazo[1,2-a]pyridin-6-yl)ethanamine (Intermediate
15) 1-(imidazo[1,2-a]pyridin-6-yl)ethanamine was prepared from
1-(imidazo[1,2-a]pyridin-6-yl)ethanone following the similar procedures
in the last two steps of thieno[3,2-c]pyridin-2-ylmethanamine, as
described above. MS (m/z): 162 (M+1)+. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 8.43
(s, 1H), 7.89 (s, 1H), 7.50-7.48 (m, 2H), 7.21 (dd, J = 9.6, 1.6 Hz, 1H),
5.35 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1H), 4.76 (m, 1H), 1.36(d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H).
