$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of
5-{[(benzo([1,3]dioxol-6-nitro)-5-ylmethyl]amino}-N-(2-[2-dimethylamino)ethyl]-
1H-benzo[de]isoquinolin-1,3(2H)-dione. 1.0 g amonafide (3.53x10-3 mol, 1
eq), 30 mL of toluene and 830 mg of 6-nitropiperonal (1.2 equivalents)
were refluxed for 16 hours. After cooling, the toluene was evaporated
under reduced pressure and the residue was directly submitted to the next
reaction. 1.62 g of the residue obtained in the first step, 10 mL of
anhydrous methanol and 445 mg NaBH3CN (2 equivalents) were stirred for 2
hours. A saturated aqueous sodium chloride solution was added and the
reaction mixture extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic phase was evaporated
under reduced pressure and the residue was submitted to flash
chromatography with CH2Cl2/MeOH (90:10 v/v), resulting in the isolation
of
5-{[(benzo([1,3]dioxol-6-nitro)-5-ylmethyl]amino}-N-(2-[2-dimethylamino)ethyl]-1H-benzo[de]isoquinolin-1,3(2H)-dione
yield 1.09 g (462.47 g/mol, 2.16x10-3 mol), 67.0%. C24H22N4O6. 1H NMR
(D6-DMSO): δ = 2.40 (6H, s, H3C-15 and H3C-16), 2.76 (2H, m, H2C- 14),
4.19 (2H, t, J = 6.6 Hz, H2C-13), 4.76 (2H, d, J = 6.0 Hz, HNH2C-18),
6.18 (2H, s, O2H2C-25), 7.10 (1H, s, HC-20), 7.16 (1H, d, J = 2.4 Hz,
H-4), 7.31 (1H, t, J = 5.9 Hz, NH-17), 7.61 (1H, t, J = 7.7 Hz, H-7),
7.75 (1H, s, HC-23), 8.02 (1H, d, J = 7.7 Hz, H-6), 8.07 (1H, d, J = 7.7
Hz, H-8), 8.08 (1H, d, J =2.4 Hz, H-2). 13C NMR (D6-DMSO): δ = 36.7
(C-13), 44.3 (C-18), 44.5 (C-15 ad C-16), 55.9 (C-14), 103.3 (C-25),
105.7, 107.3, 108.6, 120.9, 121.6, 121.8, 122.6, 125.6, 127.0, 131.8,
132.5, 133.5, 141.7, 146.6, 146.6, 152.1, 163.8 and 163.5 (C-11 and
C-12). EI-MS: 69 (81), 147 (29), 169 (100), 235 (10), 285 (10), 335 (13),
451 (less than 1) and 462 (less than 1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 2,2,2-Trichloro-N-({2-[2-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-1,3-dioxo-2,3-dihydro-1H-benzo[de]isoquinolin-
5-yl}carbamoyl)acetamide (UNBS3157), a Novel Nonhematotoxic Naphthalimide
Derivative with Potent Antitumor Activity
