$DATUM Crude aldehyde was dissolved in dry MeOH (40 mL), ACQ4 (1.01 g; 4.06
mmol) was added and mixture was stirred overnight at r.t. followed by
NaBH4 (307 mg, 8.12 mmol) added in one portion. After 5h solvent was
removed under reduced pressure and the product was purified by column
chromatography (dry flash, SiO2, eluent EA/Hex gradient 1/1 → EA, EA/MeOH
gradient 95/5 → 1/1, MeOH).
N-(3α,7α,12α-Triacetoxy-5β-cholan-24-yl)-N’-(7’-chloroquinolin-4’-yl)-butane-1,4-diamine
(14) Colorless foam softens at 80-83 ºC. [α] 20 D = +0.116 (c = 1.4×10-3
g/mL, DCM). IR (KBr): 3396w, 3304w, 2936s, 2866m, 1730s, 1610w, 1579s,
1536s, 1448w, 1370m, 1331w, 1245s, 1133w, 1068w, 1023w, 965w, 886w, 807w
cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 8.70 (d, J = 5.2 H-C(2’)), 8.12 (d, J =
2.1, H-C(8’)), 7.93 (d, J = 8.8, H-C(5’)), 7.50, (dd, J 1 = 8.9, J 2 =
2.1, H-C(6’)), 6.55 (d, J = 5.2, H-C(3’)), 6.28 (bs, H-N), 5.28 (bs, HC(
12)), 5.13-5.08 (m, H-C(7)), 4.82-4.73 (m, H-C(3)), 3.49 (t, J = 6.6,
2H-C(9’)), 2.91 (t, J = 6.7, 2H-C(12’)), 2.85-2.73 (m, 2H-C(24)), 2.31
(s, CH3COO), 2.27 (s, CH3COO), 2.24 (s, CH3COO), 1.11 (s, CH3-C(10)),
1.02 (d, J = 6.4, CH3-C(20)), 0.91 (s, CH3-C(13)). 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3, δ): 170.49, 170.33, 151.98, 150.00, 149.08, 134.68, 128.58,
124.88, 121.47, 117.30, 98.80, 75.40, 74.04, 70.67, 50.40, 49.03, 47.55,
44.99, 43.36, 43.11, 40.89, 37.71, 34.92, 34.65, 34.28, 33.32, 31.22,
28.86, 27.63, 27.25, 27.14, 26.84, 26.33, 26.20, 25.53, 22.77, 22.51,
21.55, 21.44, 21.39, 17.87, 12.19. (+)ESI-HRMS (m/z): [M + 2H]2+
376.72256 (error -2.85 ppm), [M + H]+ 752.43999 (error -4.73 ppm) ;
Combustion analysis for (C43H62ClN3O6×3H2O): calculated C 64.04, H 8.50,
N 5.21; found C 64.43, H 8.27, N 5.13. HPLC purity: Method A: RT 1.900,
area 98.59 %; method C: RT 10.694, area 99.15%.
