$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
4-[[N-(1-Tritylimidazol-4-yl)methyleneamino]-2-phenylbenzoyl]leucine
Methyl Ester. To a solution of 2-phenyl-4-aminobenzoylleucine methyl
ester hydrochloride14b (0.25 g, 0.74 mmol) in methanol was added
tritylimidazole-4-carboxaldehyde (0.25 g, 0.74 mmol) followed by 1 mL of
glacial acetic acid, and the reaction was stirred for 30 min. This was
followed by the addition of NaCNBH3 (0.046 g, 0.74 mmol), and the
reaction was stirred at room temperature for 2 h. The solvent was
evaporated, and the residue was dissolved in ethyl acetate (~3 mL) and
chromatographed on a silica gel column (1.05” × 23”). The synthesis
followed a similar procedure to that for GGTI-2132, using
2-(1-naphthyl)-4-aminobenzoylleucine methyl ester hydrochloride (0.59 g,
1.5 mmol), tritylimidazole-4-carboxaldehyde (0.61 g, 1.80 mmol), and
NaCNBH3 (0.34 g, 5.4 mmol). A white solid (0.72 g, 67%). 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) 0.13 (m, 0.8 H), 0.44 (m, 5.2 H), 0.57 (m, 2 H), 0.93 (m, 1 H),
3.40 (s, 1 H), 3.57 (s, 2 H), 4.24 (m, 1 H), 5.37-5.47 (dd, 1 H), 6.49
(s, 1 H), 7.08 (m, 2 H), 7.09-7.11 (m, 6 H), 7.30-7.32 (m, 11 H),
7.49-7.57 (m, 5 H), 7.80 (m, 2 H), 8.08 (d, 1 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Potent, highly selective, and non-thiol inhibitors of protein
geranylgeranyltransferase-I
