$DATUM (2S,5S)-2-((R)-((tert-butyldimethylsilyl)oxy)(phenyl)methyl)-5-(4-nitrobenzyl)
pyrrolidine (47a). To a solution of 4-methoxybenzyl
[(1R)-1-[(R)-{[tertbutyl(dimethyl)silyl]oxy}(phenyl)methyl]-5-(4-nitrophenyl)-4-oxopentyl]carbamate
46a (34 g, 57 mmol) in dichloromethane (200ml) was added trifluoroacetic
acid (44ml, 0.57 Mol) and the resulting mixture stirred at room
temperature for 1.5 h. The resulting dark red mixture was evaporated in
vacuo and the residue partitioned between dichloromethane (300mL) and a
saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate solution (200mL). The phases were
separated and the aqueous phase extracted with dichloromethane (2 x
200mL). The combined organic phases were dried over MgSO4, filtered and
evaporated in vacuo. The residue was then dissolved in dichloromethane
(400ml), cooled to 0°C and solid sodium triacetoxyborohydride (36.5g,
0.172Mol) was then added. The resulting mixture was allowed to warm to
room temperature with stirring for 12 h. The reaction mixture was then
carefully quenched with a saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate solution
(200mL) and the biphasic solution was stirred for 6 h. The phases were
separated and the aqueous phase extracted with dichloromethane (2 x
200mL). The combine organic phases were dried over magnesium sulfate,
filtered and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified by flash
column chromatography on a Biotage Horizon system (silica gel, 100%
hexanes to 20% EtOAc in hexanes gradient). The desired compound as clear
gum (19 g, 79%).The desired compound as clear gum (19 g, 79%). LC/MS (EI)
m/e: 427.1 (M+H)+. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ -0.16 (s, 3H), 0.03 (s, 3H),
0.86 (s, 9H), 1.48-1.27 (m, 3H), 1.81-1.76 (m, 1H), 2.02 (br s, 1H),
2.91-2.80 (m, 2H), 3.21-3.16 (m, 1H), 3.34-3.28 (m, 1H), 4.44 (d, J = 7.2
Hz, 2H), 7.31-7.23 (m, 5H), 7.42 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 8.17 (d, J = 8.4
Hz, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 60:40 to 80:20 cis:trans, 79% overall yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
