$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step G: General Procedure for Pyrrolidine Formation. To a solution of
ketones 46a-e in dichloromethane was added trifluoroacetic acid and the
resulting mixture stirred at room temperature for 1.5 h. The resulting
mixture was evaporated in vacuo and the residue partitioned between
dichloromethane and a saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate solution. The
phases were separated and the aqueous phase extracted with
dichloromethane (2×). The combined organic phases were dried over MgSO4
and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was then dissolved in
dichloromethane cooled to 0°C, and solid sodium triacetoxyborohydride was
then added. The resulting mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature
with stirring for 12 h. The reaction mixture was then carefully quenched
with a saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate solution, and the biphasic
solution was stirred for 6 h. The phases were separated, and the aqueous
phase extracted with dichloromethane (2×). The combined organic phases
were dried over MgSO4 and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified
by flash column chromatography on a Biotage Horizon system (silica gel,
100 hexanes to 20% EtOAc in hexanes gradient). The desired pyrrolidines
47a-e as clear oils.
(2S,5S)-2-((R)-((tert-butyldimethylsilyl)oxy)(3-chlorophenyl)methyl)-5-(4-nitrobenzyl)pyrrolidine
(47b). Following the procedure described for 47a, 46b (34g, 53mmol)
provided the title compound (18.45g, 74% yield) as an orange oil. 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ -0.14 (s, 3H), 0.04 (s, 3H), 0.86 (s, 9H), 1.35-1.50
(m, 3H), 1.80 (m, 1H), 2.79 (dd, J = 13.0 and 8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.88 (dd, J =
13.0 and 5.0 Hz, 1H), 3.17 (q, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 3.31 (m, 1H), 4.41 (d, J
= 7.0 Hz, 1H), 7.19 (m, 1H), 7.24 (m, 2H), 7.32 (s, 1H), 7.41 (d, J = 8.5
Hz, 2H), 8.17 (d, J 8.5 Hz, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 60:40 to 80:20 cis:trans, 74% overall yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design, Synthesis, and Evaluation of Conformationally Restricted
Acetanilides as Potent and Selective β3 Adrenergic Receptor Agonists for
the Treatment of Overactive Bladder
